    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] It is a member of the genus \"Connochaetes\" and family Bovidae.\n[2] The closest living relative of \"Tsaidamotherium\" is probably the Muskox, \"Ovibos moschatus\".\n[3] The muskox (\"Ovibos moschatus\"), also spelled musk ox and musk-ox (in Inuktitut: ᐅᒥᖕᒪᒃ, \"umingmak\" ), is an Arctic mammal of the family Bovidae, noted for its thick coat and for the strong odor emitted during the seasonal rut by males, from which its name derives.\n[4] It is a member of the Eupleridae, a family of carnivorans closely related to the mongoose family (Herpestidae)."
